{"id":"e13t1","name":"Customer Master Merge","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["crm_df","web_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Your team builds a customer master table from two feeds. The CRM feed and the web sign-up feed were designed by different teams: their columns are not in the same order, and each feed has a column the other one does not have. Both feeds send a new row every time a customer record changes, and re-ingestion sometimes produces fully duplicated rows.</p>\n<p>Implement <code>solve</code> so that it returns one row per customer with the latest known version of the record.</p>\n<h3>Input</h3>\n<p><code>crm_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>may contain spaces and mixed case; may be null or empty</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>full_name</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>may be null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>email</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>free text; may be null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>updated_at</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>format <code>yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss</code>, never null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>web_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>updated_at</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>format <code>yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss</code>, never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>may contain spaces and mixed case; may be null or empty</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>email</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>free text; may be null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>phone</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>may be null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Combine all rows of both feeds. A column that exists in only one feed is null for the rows coming from the other feed.</li>\n<li>Every row gets a <code>source</code> column: <code>\"crm\"</code> for rows of <code>crm_df</code>, <code>\"web\"</code> for rows of <code>web_df</code>.</li>\n<li><code>customer_id</code> is normalized by trimming spaces and converting to uppercase. Rows whose normalized <code>customer_id</code> is null or empty are dropped.</li>\n<li><code>email</code> is normalized by trimming spaces and converting to lowercase (null stays null).</li>\n<li>For each <code>customer_id</code>, keep only the row with the greatest <code>updated_at</code>. If a CRM row and a web row share the greatest <code>updated_at</code>, the CRM row wins. Rows of the same feed with the same <code>customer_id</code> and the same <code>updated_at</code> are identical copies.</li>\n<li>All other columns are returned exactly as they are in the kept row (no merging of values across rows).</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>A DataFrame with exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>full_name</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>email</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>phone</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>source</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>updated_at</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>customer_id</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>crm_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>full_name</th>\n<th>email</th>\n<th>updated_at</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\" c1 \"</td>\n<td>Amina Alaoui</td>\n<td>\"Amina@Mail.com \"</td>\n<td>2024-03-01 10:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\"C2\"</td>\n<td>Youssef Bennani</td>\n<td>youssef@mail.com</td>\n<td>2024-03-02 09:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\"C3\"</td>\n<td>Salma Kettani</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>2024-03-01 08:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>web_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>updated_at</th>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>email</th>\n<th>phone</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>2024-03-05 12:00:00</td>\n<td>\"C1\"</td>\n<td>\" amina.new@mail.com\"</td>\n<td>+212600000001</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2024-03-02 09:00:00</td>\n<td>\"c2\"</td>\n<td>YOUSSEF@web.com</td>\n<td>+212600000002</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2024-03-03 10:00:00</td>\n<td>\"C4\"</td>\n<td>omar@mail.com</td>\n<td>null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2024-03-04 10:00:00</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>ghost@mail.com</td>\n<td>+212600000009</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>full_name</th>\n<th>email</th>\n<th>phone</th>\n<th>source</th>\n<th>updated_at</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>C1</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>amina.new@mail.com</td>\n<td>+212600000001</td>\n<td>web</td>\n<td>2024-03-05 12:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C2</td>\n<td>Youssef Bennani</td>\n<td>youssef@mail.com</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>crm</td>\n<td>2024-03-02 09:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C3</td>\n<td>Salma Kettani</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>crm</td>\n<td>2024-03-01 08:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C4</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>omar@mail.com</td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>web</td>\n<td>2024-03-03 10:00:00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Function signature</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">from pyspark.sql import DataFrame\n\ndef solve(crm_df: DataFrame, web_df: DataFrame) -&gt; DataFrame:\n    ...\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the PySpark DataFrame API. Do not convert to pandas and do not call <code>collect()</code> or <code>toPandas()</code> inside <code>solve</code>.</li>\n<li>Each feed has up to 10^6 rows.</li>\n<li>Either input DataFrame may be empty. The returned DataFrame may be empty; its columns and types must still match the specification.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import DataFrame, Window\nfrom pyspark.sql import functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(crm_df: DataFrame, web_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return crm_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°5, question 1","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"crm_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"customer_id string, full_name string, email string, updated_at string","rows":[[" c1 ","Amina Alaoui","Amina@Mail.com ","2024-03-01 10:00:00"],["C2","Youssef Bennani","youssef@mail.com","2024-03-02 09:00:00"],["C3","Salma Kettani",null,"2024-03-01 08:00:00"]]}},"web_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"updated_at string, customer_id string, email string, phone string","rows":[["2024-03-05 12:00:00","C1"," amina.new@mail.com","+212600000001"],["2024-03-02 09:00:00","c2","YOUSSEF@web.com","+212600000002"],["2024-03-03 10:00:00","C4","omar@mail.com",null],["2024-03-04 10:00:00",null,"ghost@mail.com","+212600000009"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","full_name","email","phone","source","updated_at"],"rows":[["C1",null,"amina.new@mail.com","+212600000001","web","2024-03-05 12:00:00"],["C2","Youssef Bennani","youssef@mail.com",null,"crm","2024-03-02 09:00:00"],["C3","Salma Kettani",null,null,"crm","2024-03-01 08:00:00"],["C4",null,"omar@mail.com",null,"web","2024-03-03 10:00:00"]]}}],"hidden_n":4,"hidden":"","solution":""}